#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trust Model (Required Reading for Open-Source Deployment)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:13
msgid "FreeAnima is designed for **single-user local / intranet** deployment:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/security.md:17
msgid ""
"Business HTTP API (`/api/*` except health/CORS/echo) requires a **Service "
"API Token** (`Authorization: Bearer fa_at_…`); create with `anima token "
"create`. Binding `127.0.0.1` limits network exposure but does not replace "
"token auth — any local process that can reach the port still needs a valid "
"token for business routes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/security.md:17
msgid ""
"Default bind is `127.0.0.1`; for LAN access, assess CORS and network "
"isolation yourself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guide/security.md:17
msgid ""
"**Do not** expose the service to the public internet without TLS and token-"
"protected clients (see [`remote-access.md`](remote-access.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "Credential Responsibilities"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Rule                     | Description                                                                                                                                                          |\n"
"| ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Sole authoritative store | **Vault** (ECS `vault_item` in User + Agent libraries); legacy pass (`~/.password-store`) is read-only on disk after migration — runtime no longer uses pass CLI     |\n"
"| Never commit secrets     | Do not write API keys, tokens, DB passwords into `config.yaml` and commit to git; runtime LLM/MCP settings live in PG — use `vault()` / `env()` references there too |\n"
"| Runtime directory        | `~/.anima/` (`FREEANIMA_HOME` overridable) holds config, agent machine key (`vault/agent-machine.key`), conversations, memory—recommend `chmod 700`                  |\n"
"| CLI plaintext output     | `anima vault get` prints Agent-library field plaintext to stdout; do not redirect to shared logs                                                                     |\n"
"| User master password     | Set only in Shell `/vault` or bundled Chat unlock box; **never** sent as a chat message or stored in PG messages                                                     |\n"
"| Chat User vault unlock   | **v1 bundled Chat only** (`src/app/shell/web` / desktop / mobile); Discord / WeChat gateways cannot unlock User library                                              |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:30
msgid ""
"`config.yaml` supports `vault(\"item_id\", \"field\")` (Agent library, Hub "
"headless) and `env(\"KEY\")` for secrets; values are injected at runtime. "
"User-library inject for tools requires an unlocked Chat session on the "
"client."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/guide/security.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Vault trust boundaries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Surface | User library                | Agent library                         |\n"
"| ------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Hub PG  | Ciphertext + verifier only  | Ciphertext + machine key file on disk |\n"
"| LLM     | Metadata / inject ack only  | Metadata / inject ack only            |\n"
"| Shell   | Client master key in memory | Hub decrypt over loopback SAP         |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "Data Persistence"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Path                               | Content                  | Encryption                      |\n"
"| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------- |\n"
"| PostgreSQL conversation archive    | conversations / messages | No application-layer encryption |\n"
"| `~/.anima/vault/agent-machine.key` | Agent vault machine key  | File permissions (`chmod 600`)  |\n"
"| `~/.anima/weixin/`                 | WeChat sync state        | None                            |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:48
msgid "Disk backup = data access. Protect backup media accordingly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "LLM Tool Risks"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:61
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Capability                    | Risk                                                                                                                              |\n"
"| ----------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| `terminal`                    | Default `shell: true`, can run arbitrary shell commands                                                                           |\n"
"| `file_read_file`              | Partial path deny (`.ssh` private keys, `/etc/passwd`, etc.); **not** full `/etc/` deny                                           |\n"
"| `file_write_file`             | deny list + write-protected paths                                                                                                 |\n"
"| MCP tools                     | Capabilities entirely determined by external Server; stdio default, SSE auth scheme not fully defined                             |\n"
"| Capability mask (Mask)        | Conversation-level tool whitelist; `deny` overrides `allow`; LLM cannot see policy details; see `src/capabilities/task/src/mask/` |\n"
"| ACP (Cursor)                  | Default **auto-approve** all `session/request_permission` (`allow-once`)                                                          |\n"
"| `vault_list` / `vault_search` | Agent vault metadata only; no secret values                                                                                       |\n"
"| `vault_inject_env`            | Injects runtime env for subprocesses; tool result is ack only; User library requires Chat unlock                                  |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measures in Place"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Measure                 | Description                                                                                                                            |\n"
"| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Same-origin RPC         | TanStack Start server functions same-origin by default, no CORS whitelist needed                                                       |\n"
"| Config secret redaction | `AppRuntime.getConfig()` → `sanitizeConfigForApi()` (`api_key`, `database.url`, nested `pushkey`, `mcp env`, etc.)                     |\n"
"| MCP config redaction    | `sanitizeMcpConfig`: `env` exposes only `env_keys`                                                                                     |\n"
"| Write path safety       | `file_write_file` deny list (partial `/etc/*`, `.ssh` private keys, etc.)                                                              |\n"
"| Slash commands          | Whitelist routing; every command must produce user-visible feedback; long-running commands send an immediate ack then the final result |\n"
"| MCP default stdio       | Reduces port exposure                                                                                                                  |\n"
"| Vault isolation         | LLM sees vault item metadata only, not decrypted fields                                                                                |\n"
"| Service API Token       | Business `/api/*` routes require `Authorization: Bearer fa_at_…` (`service_api_tokens` PG table); health/CORS/echo exempt              |\n"
"| CI secret scanning      | `.github/workflows/security.yml` (Gitleaks); GitHub Secret scanning + Push protection (free for public repos)                          |\n"
"| `.gitignore`            | `.env.*`, `config.yaml`, private key suffixes                                                                                          |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "Known Gaps (Documentation ≠ Fully Implemented)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:80
msgid ""
"The following are planned in code or docs—**deployers must not assume "
"implemented**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:90
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Priority | Item                                                  | Status                              |\n"
"| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n"
"| P0       | file_read_file full deny (`/etc/` etc.)               | Partial                             |\n"
"| P0       | `terminal_run` / `code_execute` default `shell=False` | Not implemented                     |\n"
"| P1       | Runtime Unix socket `chmod 600` + handshake token     | Not implemented                     |\n"
"| P1       | `FREEANIMA_WRITE_SAFE_ROOT` / `READ_SAFE_ROOT`        | Not implemented                     |\n"
"| P2       | Config redaction maintenance for new secret fields    | Partial — sync on new config fields |\n"
"| P3       | IPC / LLM rate limiting                               | None                                |\n"
"| P3       | Session disk encryption                               | None                                |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "Threat Sources"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:100
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Code  | Name                | Description                                                      |\n"
"| ----- | ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **A** | External attack     | Unauthorized access, port exposure                               |\n"
"| **B** | LLM-layer injection | Prompt injection, tool parameter manipulation, command injection |\n"
"| **C** | Agent error         | Mistaken dangerous operations                                    |\n"
"| **D** | Dependency chain    | Third-party lib / MCP / ACP compromise                           |\n"
"| **E** | Data security       | Conversation leak, key leak, memory tampering                    |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guide/security.md:101
#, no-wrap
msgid "Security Matrix"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guide/security.md:111
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Module             | A External                                                 | B LLM injection                                                     | C Agent error             | D Dependencies     | E Data                             |\n"
"| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n"
"| **Runtime**        | Default 127.0.0.1 bind                                     | MaxTurnsExceeded                                                    | Gap: rate limiting        | llm client vulns   | PG unencrypted                     |\n"
"| **Gateway**        | Token in Vault / env                                       | Malicious messages                                                  | Reply with sensitive info | SDK vulns          | —                                  |\n"
"| **CLI / Tools**    | Local shell compromised                                    | file_read_file partial deny (**P0 extending**); shell=True (**P0**) | rm -rf etc.               | —                  | Logs may contain conversations     |\n"
"| **HTTP / Console** | `service_api_tokens` Bearer token（所有来源，含 loopback） | BFF does not touch LLM params directly                              | config display            | Vue/axios          | SSE plaintext                      |\n"
"| **MCP / ACP**      | SSE auth undefined                                         | Malicious params                                                    | Wrong delegation          | Server compromised | Context may contain sensitive data |\n"
"| **Vault**          | Agent machine key file permissions                         | Metadata-only tools; inject ack                                     | Wrong item inject         | Web Crypto         | User MP never in PG messages       |\n"
msgstr ""

